From 1088a1b3ef19a54499abbf630360af9a75062bbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:24:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Bugfix: handle default values in MeTiS v5 option arrays
 [report R. Perry]

In MeTiS v5, option value -1 means "use the default value", and
callers commonly fill their option array with -1. The v5 routines used
`options[METIS_OPTION_NUMBERING]` as the base value without any check,
so that such callers had their graphs built with a base value of -1,
which led to invalid memory accesses and endless loops in coarsening.

`_SCOTCH_METIS_optionGet()` now reads option values, substituting the
default value when the option array is missing or when the value is
-1, and the numbering option is checked to be 0 or 1 in all v5
routines, as well as in `METIS_PartMeshDual()`.

Refs: CLI-06
